 "title": "Hardness needs a flat disc, not roundness",
 "subject": "What the knot's resolution-hard contradiction on two-kind spheres needs from the sphere's shape",
 "conclusion": "On every two-kind knot sphere the flat states and the Sperner reduction need only a corner-free disc whose rim reaches the six corners, so the knot's contradiction needs resolution width at least a constant times that disc's radius and at most O(sqrt n). Hardness therefore follows the largest flat disc, not roundness: spheres with a flat disc of radius order sqrt(n) are hard without any witness.",
